Packaging (done in 0.1.0)
  * Package name v7unix-toolchain; GNU autotools (configure.ac + Makefile.am).
  * Install layout: host binaries under $(libexecdir)/v7unix (original names);
    v7cc/v7as/v7ld symlinks in $(bindir); target runtime in $(libdir)/v7unix;
    manpages in a v7unix section; future headers in $(includedir)/v7unix.
  * dist/ template tree + README.distributions for 10 distributions.

Remaining
  * froot1 (the minimal self-hosting root) is DONE: tools/mkfroot.sh + `make
    froot1` / `make froot1-dist`, verified by tools/selfhost.sh (compiles the
    toolchain subset cc/as/ld + friends from orig/).
  * froot2 — froot1 + whatever else it takes to build the whole /usr/src tree.
  Step 1 — build the toolchain, pure C: make, yacc, cp, rm, cmp, touch, ls,
  diff (all pure C; cc/cpp/c0/c1/c2/as/as2/ld already done).
  Step 2 — toolchain .s: none.
  Step 3 — whole tree, pure C: lex, sh, sed, tar, tp, grep, mv, ln, mkdir,
  chmod, chown, cat, echo, pr, strip, size, install, du, and the rest.
  Step 4 — whole tree, assembly: factor, primes, bas, roff, standalone.

  * Port yacc, make to modern/ (source is in orig/; c99/ needs only the
    .c/.h modernization — c99/ mirrors orig/ except .c/.h).
  * Port the basic build utilities too (rm, cp, cmp, touch, ls, diff, mv, ln,
    mkdir, chmod, chown, cat, echo, pr) with original V7 behavior, not host
    equivalents.
  * lex: not needed for the toolchain itself (orig/ has no .l files); needed
    for the whole tree (awk + struct) — see CROSSCOMPILE.md §5.
  * adb: target-resident, never a host binary — modernize to the pcc/PDP-11
    dialect only (PORTING.md §7 bucket 2).
  * Build V7 libc from source (orig/libc) to replace the shipped libc.a.
  * Ship V7 reference binaries (orig/bin, orig/lib) for byte-comparison.
  * Headers: install V7 target headers under $(includedir)/v7unix.
  * Port mkfs and fsck to the modern host (kept in this repo; filsys depends
    on it for them).
  * Scope rule: port to modern/ (host C) only what *executes* on the host.
    crt0.o / fcrt0.o / mcrt0.o / fmcrt0.o / libc.a are linked, never run
    standalone, and stay as PDP-11 assembler/objects.
